Package: foodnet
Title: Receive foodnet Consumer-Resource Model Parameters in R
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: person("The foodnet authors", role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "noreply@example.com")
Description: Receives consumer-resource model parameters from foodnet, the tool that derives which
    taxon produces and which consumes which metabolite from mGrowthDB batch monocultures, either by
    listening on a local port for the page's "Send to R" button or by fetching them from the page
    itself. The parameters are measured amounts (net changes in mM over a growth phase), the growth
    rates of the same cultures and the medium's initial concentrations, and they arrive with their
    caveats as data: which cells were never assayed, which links were seen only in another medium and
    so have no size, which values pool experiments that disagree, and which taxa have no growth rate.
    Those caveats are printed on arrival and acted on when an efficiency matrix is built, and a
    missing growth rate stops a simulation rather than passing unnoticed. The package assumes no
    simulator: it hands over plain matrices and vectors, with a helper that shapes them for miaSim.
License: Apache License (== 2)
URL: https://github.com/hallucigenia-sparsa/foodnet
BugReports: https://github.com/hallucigenia-sparsa/foodnet/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports: jsonlite, utils
